{"additions":252,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds an optional top-level config node `projects-board` that pins the Projects page to one board — by title (case-insensitive) or by project number. Absent, the page behaves exactly as before.\n\n```kdl\nprojects-board \"vig demo board\"\n// or by project number:\nprojects-board 2\n```\n\nWhen set:\n\n- The page shows only the matching linked project; the selection is fixed.\n- `p` / `P` no longer cycle — pressing them shows `board pinned by config (projects-board)` in the status bar.\n- The header shows the pinned board's title without the `(i/n)` counter.\n- If no linked project matches, the board pane shows a notice naming the pin, e.g. `projects-board \"foo\" does not match any project linked to this repository`.\n\nCloses #131\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/core/config/loader.rs`** — new `ProjectsBoard` enum (`ByTitle(String)` / `ByNumber(u64)`) with `matches()` and a `Display` impl that renders the pin as written (`\"foo\"` / `2`); accessor `Config::projects_board() -> Result<Option<ProjectsBoard>>` validating exactly one argument (string or positive integer, no properties) with the config path in the error; validated in `with_user`.\n- **`src/core/config/merge.rs`** — `projects-board` added to the replace-wholesale top-level nodes and to the unknown-block error text.\n- **`src/core/config/mod.rs`** — re-export `ProjectsBoard`.\n- **`src/projects/state.rs`** — `ProjectsState` reads the pin; the linked-project list (from `gh repo view` and the disk cache) is filtered to the pinned project, so the selection, header and board follow it; `p` / `P` short-circuit into a status message; `update_notice` names an unmatched pin. The disk cache still stores the full unfiltered list.\n- **`docs/config.md`** — merge-rule row, schema line, and a `### projects-board` section with both forms.\n- **`README.md` / `docs/README.ja.md`** — one-line mention in the Projects View section.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Loader: parsing both forms, and rejection of no/extra args, a property, an empty title, non-positive numbers, a float and a boolean (error names `projects-board` and the config file path).\n- Merge: `projects-board` replaces the default node wholesale; unknown-block error text lists it.\n- State: pin by title is case-insensitive and fixes the selection (header label `(1, 1)`, `p` / `P` set the status message instead of cycling); pin by number selects that project; an unmatched pin shows the naming notice.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- No tape/GIF change: the default demo flow is unchanged — the demo repo has one linked project and no pin is added to the demo, so `tape/demo-projects.tape` replays identically.\n- Not exercised against a live `gh` with multiple linked projects; behaviour is covered by the state tests above.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":7,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:52:00Z","deletions":15,"headRefName":"feat/projects-board-pin","labels":[],"number":134,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLc7Zpw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe documentation currently describes a status message that does not match the implemented `PINNED_MESSAGE`, which should be corrected before approval.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds a new top-level `projects-board` config node to optionally pin the Projects page to a single GitHub Project (by title or project number), disabling project cycling and updating UI messaging/docs accordingly while preserving existing behavior when unset.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces `ProjectsBoard` parsing/validation in config loading, plus merge behavior and re-exports.\n- Updates Projects page state to filter linked projects by the configured pin and short-circuit `p`/`P` cycling into a status message.\n- Documents the new config option in `docs/config.md` and mentions it in the English/Japanese READMEs.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Applies the pin to the linked-project list, disables cycling when pinned, and adds notice/status messaging + tests. |\r\n| src/core/config/mod.rs | Re-exports `ProjectsBoard` from the loader module. |\r\n| src/core/config/merge.rs | Treats `projects-board` as a replace-wholesale top-level node and updates merge error text + tests. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Adds `ProjectsBoard` type plus `Config::projects_board()` parsing/validation and tests. |\r\n| README.md | Mentions the new `projects-board` capability in the Projects view section. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Mentions `projects-board` in the Japanese Projects view section. |\r\n| docs/config.md | Documents `projects-board` syntax/behavior and adds it to the merge-rules table/schema. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 7/7 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T05:54:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c4c9761d3071ea4a262458f7c8ef29a442234d14"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLc8pxQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T05:58:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c4c9761d3071ea4a262458f7c8ef29a442234d14"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLc8qUQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T05:58:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c4c9761d3071ea4a262458f7c8ef29a442234d14"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLc89Cw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T05:59:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c4c9761d3071ea4a262458f7c8ef29a442234d14"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLc9tkA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe current pin-filtering logic can still yield multiple matching projects, which undermines the “pinned to one board / selection fixed” behavior.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/core/config/loader.rs:474**\n* The validation error detail `a project number is positive` is ungrammatical and reads like a statement rather than a constraint. Rewording it improves the resulting user-facing error message.\n```\n                _ => Err(invalid(\"a project number is positive\")),\n```\n**src/projects/state.rs:325**\n* `apply_pin` can return multiple projects if the pin matches more than one linked project (e.g., duplicate titles or project-number collisions across owners). That breaks the “pinned to one board / selection fixed” behavior and can re-enable the `(i/n)` counter while still disabling `p`/`P`. Consider limiting the filtered list to a single match (first match) so the UI remains consistently pinned.\n```\n            Some(pin) => projects\n                .into_iter()\n                .filter(|p| pin.matches(p.number, &p.title))\n                .collect(),\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 7/7 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:02:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"e6bfee33d78160559980410d093f581c98f2a605"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLc-W5A","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:04:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"e6bfee33d78160559980410d093f581c98f2a605"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLc-XgA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:04:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"e6bfee33d78160559980410d093f581c98f2a605"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:07:27Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33362937301/job/99397726489","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:07:28Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:01:24Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33362467719/job/99396369826","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:00:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:00:48Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33362467729/job/99396369766","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:00:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:01:12Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/action